nt URL and credential object, e.g. new BlobServiceClient(url, credential) or new SecretClient(vaultUrl, credential). No legacy constructor patterns or connection string-based construction when identity-based auth is available.\n4. **Async/Await Pattern** — Uses async/await for all asynchronous operations. No raw .then()/.catch() chains when await is cleaner. No callback-based patterns. Top-level async function or IIFE for entry point.\n5. **Pagination with for-await-of** — List/query operations use for-await-of iteration over the PagedAsyncIterableIterator returned by SDK methods. Does not collect all pages into an array in memory (e.g., no Array.from() or manual page accumulation). Uses byPage() when per-page control is needed.\n6. **LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)** — Long-running operations use the begin* method prefix (e.g., beginDeleteSecret, beginCreateOrUpdate) and await poller.pollUntilDone(). No manual setTimeout/setInterval polling loops.\n7. **RestError Exception Handling** — Catches RestError (from @azure/core-rest-pipeline or the service package) with statusCode inspection for error-specific handling. Not just generic Error or try/catch without type checking.\n8. **No Deprecated Packages** — No deprecated or legacy Azure packages in package.json: azure-storage, azure-arm-*, ms-rest-azure, @azure/ms-rest-js, @azure/ms-rest-nodeauth, @azure/ms-rest-azure-js. All dependencies use the current @azure/* track.\n9. **Logging via @azure/logger** — Uses @azure/logger with setLogLevel() or the AZURE_LOG_LEVEL environment variable for SDK diagnostic logging. No custom logging wrappers around SDK internals.\n10. **package.json with Correct Dependencies** — Includes a valid package.json with all required @azure/* dependencies listed. TypeScript projects include tsconfig.json and appropriate @types/* packages or use a recent TypeScript version with built-in types.\n\n### Prompt-Specific Criteria\n\nThe generated code should include:\r\n- `@azure/cosmos` npm package\r\n- `CosmosClient` constructor with endpoint and key\r\n- `client.databases.createIfNotExists()` and `database.containers.createIfNotExists()`\r\n- `container.items.create()`, `container.item(id, partitionKey).read()`\r\n- `container.items.query()` with `SqlQuerySpec`\r\n- `container.item(id, partitionKey).replace()` and `.delete()`\r\n- `FeedResponse` iteration and error status codes\n\n## Generated Code\n\n### README.md\n```\n# Azure Cosmos DB CRUD Operations (TypeScript)\r\n\r\nThis program demonstrates CRUD operations on an Azure Cosmos DB NoSQL container using TypeScript.\r\n\r\n## Required Package\r\n\r\n- **@azure/cosmos** (v4.0.0+): Official Azure Cosmos DB SDK for Node.js/TypeScript\r\n\r\n## Setup\r\n\r\n1. Install dependencies:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   npm install\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n2. Set environment variables with your Cosmos DB credentials:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   # Windows (PowerShell)\r\n   $env:COSMOS_ENDPOINT=\"https://your-account.documents.azure.com:443/\"\r\n   $env:COSMOS_KEY=\"your-cosmos-db-key\"\r\n\r\n   # Linux/Mac\r\n   export COSMOS_ENDPOINT=\"https://your-account.documents.azure.com:443/\"\r\n   export COSMOS_KEY=\"your-cosmos-db-key\"\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n3. Build the TypeScript code:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   npm run build\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n4. Run the program:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   npm start\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n## What the Program Does\r\n\r\n1. **Create CosmosClient**: Initializes the client with endpoint and key\r\n2. **Create Database \u0026 Container**: Creates \"TestDB\" database and \"Items\" container with partition key \"/category\"\r\n3. **Create Item**: Inserts a new item with id, category, name, and quantity (Status 201)\r\n4. **Read Item**: Retrieves the item using item().read() (Status 200)\r\n5. **Query Items**: Executes parameterized query for items with category=\"electronics\"\r\n6. **Replace Item**: Updates the item's quantity using item().replace() (Status 200)\r\n7. **Delete Item**: Removes the item using item().delete() (Status 204)\